  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 404.09 Modifications and Expansions",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 404.09 Modifications and Expansions.\n\n(a) Any person seeking to expand a large CWS shall submit the following to the department:\n\n(1) A water audit conducted in accordance with the standards of the AWWA;\n\n(2) The proposed increase in average day and maximum day demand due to the proposed expansion; and\n\n(3) Documentation demonstrating the existing source(s) have the required supply capacity as required by Env-Dw 404.04 and Env-Dw 404.05.\n\n(b) Any person seeking to modify or expand a large CWS in accordance with Env-Dw 404.02 above shall submit the following to the department:\n\n(1) A description of the proposed modifications or expansions;\n\n(2) An explanation of why the modifications or expansions are needed;\n\n(3) Plan sheets, including revisions to previously approved plans, and specifications for the proposed modifications or expansion as required by Env-Dw 404.04 and Env-Dw 404.05;\n\n(4) Revised calculations, as applicable;\n\n(5) If infrastructure is decommissioned, photo documentation showing a minimum 12-inch gap in the piping from the original well(s), storage tank(s), and any other decommissioned infrastructure;\n\n(6) If connection to another PWS is proposed, documentation from the supplying owner certifying that:\n\na. Adequate quantities of water are available to serve the proposed PWS; and\n\nb. With the proposed PWS online, adequate system pressures and source capacity will be maintained in the supplying PWS; and\n\n(7) The application fee as required by Env-Dw 402.03.\n\n(c) For deepening or hydrofracturing of wells at CWSs, the applicant shall comply with Env-Dw 302 and Env-Dw 305, as applicable.\n\n(d) Replacement in-kind shall not require department approval, except that replacement of a well shall comply with the requirements of Env-Dw 302 or Env-Dw 305, as applicable.\n\n(e) The plans and specifications for modifications to large CWSs shall be sealed by a professional engineer licensed in the state of New Hampshire.\n\n(f) The department shall approve the application to modify the CWS if the design meets the criteria in this part.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for Env-Dw 404) #10611, eff 6-1-14\n\nNew. #14158, eff 12-25-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw400.html"
}
